# tools/r/rune_assert_sweep.rish — the rune assert sweep audit.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/r/rune_assert_sweep.rish
#
# Sweeps authored Rye for assert coverage — the TAME "say your invariants" floor.
# Two tiers, matching TAME's own gate-vs-ratchet split:
#   * GATE (fails RED): core module files that carry asserts must keep them — a
#     regression guard. A gated file dropping to zero asserts fails the audit.
#   * ADVISE (prints, never fails): the wider sweep names zero-assert modules as
#     migrate-on-touch candidates, without gating.
# Seated 20260810 on Keaton's word; widened across modules from the Mandate seed.

say "rune-assert-sweep: Language EN — audit assert coverage across authored Rye."
say "rune-assert-sweep: Style Radiant — gate the asserting cores; advise the rest."
say "rune-assert-sweep: Lens TAME — a gated module says its invariants; a ratchet names the gaps."

# --- GATE: core modules that carry asserts today (regression guard) ---
let gate = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/rune_assert_sweep_scan.sh" "mandate/store.rye" "mandate/keyed.rye" "tally/seed.rye" "tally/gardens.rye" "tally/kumara.rye" "caravan/seed.rye" "caravan/bounded.rye" "comlink/topology.rye" "kumara/tilak.rye" "settlement/constellation.rye" "sundial/sundial.rye" "glow/expr.rye"]
say gate.out
# values_apart: the verdict key and the exit status must agree.
assert gate.out contains "verdict=ok" else "rune-assert-sweep: a gated core module dropped to zero asserts"
assert gate.ok else "rune-assert-sweep: the verdict reads ok while the status fails — they must agree"

# The advise tier is empty for now — every surveyed module carries asserts and is
# gated. The scan keeps its `advise` mode for the next module that opts in before it
# has earned its asserts.

say "GREEN: rune-assert-sweep — twelve gated cores keep their asserts; the advise tier is empty"
